#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:1
msgid "The SME Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:3
msgid ""
"The SME structure contains all the information necessary to run PySME.   "
"It is by design similar to the IDL structure of SME, but with a lot of "
"changes for ease of use. Note that some parameters depend on the number "
"of segments in the observation. When creating a new structure it is "
"therefore recommended to define the wavelengths first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:9
msgid "Stellar Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:11
msgid ""
"Stellar parameters describe the star in general and are usually what we "
"want to fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:13
msgid "`teff`: The effective temperature of the star in **Kelvin**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:14
msgid "`logg`: The surface gravity of the star in log (cgs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:15
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`monh`: The overall metallicity of the star in log₁₀ relative to the "
"individual abundances (see {ref}`abund`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:16
msgid ""
"`vsini`: The (projected) rotation velocity in km s⁻¹. Describes the "
"rotational broadening."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:17
msgid "If `vsini` is non-zero, you should set several values for `mu`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:18
msgid ""
"`vmic`: The micro-turbulence velocity in km s⁻¹. Describes turbulence on "
"scales **smaller** than the photon mean free path, adding additional line"
" broadening."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:19
msgid ""
"`vmac`: The macro-turbulence velocity in km s⁻¹. Describes turbulence on "
"scales **larger** than the photon mean free path, also contributing to "
"broadening."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:20
msgid ""
"`mu`: Limb-angle values ($\\mu = \\cos\\theta$) at which the radiative-"
"transfer calculation is performed. $\\mu = 1$ corresponds to disk center,"
" $0$ to the limb."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:22
msgid "Radial velocity and Continuum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:24
msgid ""
"The radial velocity and continuum shift the continuum in wavelength and "
"intensity direction respectively. How to best handle them often depends "
"on the situation and the quality of the observation data. Therefore PySME"
" has many options to determine them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:30
msgid ""
"`cscale`: The polynomial parameters for each segment, that are applied to"
" the synthetic spectrum to match the observation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:31
msgid ""
"The polynomial is calculated using the wavelength grid of the "
"observation, shifted so that the first point is 0. I.e. the polynomial is"
" f(wave - wave[0])."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:32
msgid ""
"`vrad`: The radial velocity in km/s that was applied to each segment of "
"the synthethized spectrum to match the observation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:33
msgid ""
"`cscale_flag`: Determines how the continuum is fitted, or if it is fitted"
" at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:34
msgid "none: No continuum correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:35
msgid "fix: Use whatever continuum scale has been set, but don't change it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:36
msgid "constant: scale everything by a factor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:37
msgid "linear: First order polynomial, i.e. a straight line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:38
msgid "quadratic: Second order polynomial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:39
msgid ""
"`vrad_flag`: Determines how the radial velocity is fitted, or if it is "
"fitted at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:40
msgid "none: No radial velocity fitting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:41
msgid "fix: Use the set value for the radial velocity, but don't change it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:42
msgid "each: Fit each wavelength segment individally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:43
msgid "whole: Fit the whole spectrum at once"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:46
msgid "Spectra"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:48
msgid ""
"Spectra are given as a list of arrays[^iliffe], where each array "
"represents one wavelength segment of the spectrum. If there is only one "
"segment, the list will only have one element. For legacy reasons there is"
" also an interface to the 'old' system and names (e.g. smod instead of "
"synth) from IDL SME. It is recommend however to use the new variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:54
msgid "wave"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:54
msgid "The wavelength grid of the observation and/or the synthetic spectrum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:55
msgid "spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:55
msgid "The observed spectrum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:56
msgid "uncs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:57
msgid ""
"The uncertainties of the observed spectrum. If None will use uncertainty "
"1 for all points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:59
msgid "mask"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:60
msgid ""
"The pixel mask for the observation, with defination of 0 as bad pixel, 1 "
"as line pixel, 2 as continuum pixel, and 4 as vrad pixel. The masks are "
"additive, i.e., you can set mask value to 5 for line and vrad pixel. Only"
" the good pixels will contribute to the fit, but the synthetic spectrum "
"will still be calculated. Note that ``dtype`` of ``sme.mask`` must be "
"int."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:62
msgid "synth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:62
msgid "The synthetic spectrum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:64
msgid "wran"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:65
msgid ""
"The first and last wavelength of each segment. You only need this if you "
"dont have an observation and dont want to specify the exact wavelength "
"grid of the synthetic observation. Note that this is not an Illiffe "
"vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:69
msgid "wint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:70
msgid ""
"Optional wavelength grid passed to SMElib `Transf` as adaptive grid for "
"each segment. Accepts the same segment-aware input styles as `wave`: "
"`numpy.ndarray` (single segment), `list` of arrays (multi-segment), or "
"`Iliffe_vector`. If provided, `sme.wint[segment]` is used directly for "
"synthesis. If not provided, PySME can reuse an internal cached adaptive "
"grid when `reuse_wavelength_grid=True`; otherwise SMElib computes a new "
"adaptive grid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:80
msgid "Abundance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:82
msgid ""
"The individal abundances are stored in a seperate Abundance object, which"
" shares the same metallicity as the overall structure. For more detailed "
"information see [](abundance)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:86
msgid "abund"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:86
msgid "The abundance object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:88
msgid "Linelist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:90
msgid ""
"The sme structure does contain the whole linelist in the linelist "
"property. For legacy reasons, it also provides direct access to the "
"'species' and 'atomic' arrays. They refer directly to the linelist "
"however. For more detailed information see "
"[](../fundamentals/linelist.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:95
msgid "linelist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:95
msgid "The linelist object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:96
msgid "species"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:96
msgid "Names of the species of each spectral line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:97
msgid "atomic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:98
msgid ""
"Atomic linelist data with columns \"atom_number\", \"ionization\", "
"\"wlcent\", \"excit\", \"gflog\", \"gamrad\", \"gamqst\", \"gamvw\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:101
msgid "Atmosphere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:103
msgid ""
"Unlike the linelist the atmosphere is stored in an external file, that is"
" only referenced by name in the structure. For more detailed information "
"see [](atmosphere)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:107
msgid "atmo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:107
msgid "The atmosphere object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:109
msgid "NLTE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:111
msgid ""
"Unlike the linelist, but similar to the atmosphere, the NLTE parameters "
"are stored in external tables, which are only referenced by name. For "
"more detailed information see [](nlte)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:115
msgid "nlte"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:115
msgid "The NLTE object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:117
msgid "Instrument Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:119
msgid ""
"PySME can also model instrumental broadening as part of the spectral "
"synthesis. For this you need to specify the resolution and the broadening"
" method to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:123
msgid "ipres"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:123
msgid "The resolution of the instrument to simulate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:124
msgid "iptype"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:125
msgid ""
"The broadening profile of the instrument. One of \"gauss\", \"sinc\", "
"\"table\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:127
msgid "ip_x"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:128
msgid ""
"The x points of the instrument profile. Only relevant if iptype is "
"'table'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:130
msgid "ip_y"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:131
msgid ""
"The y points of the instrument profile. Only relevant if iptype is "
"'table'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:134
msgid "Fitresults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:136
msgid "fitparameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:137
msgid ""
"The fitparameters used for the fitting. See "
"[fitparameters](../concepts/fitparameters.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:139
msgid "fitresults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:139
msgid "The fitresults object. See [fitresults](../concepts/fitresults.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:141
msgid "System Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:143
msgid ""
"The sme structure does contain information about the host system. E.g. "
"which operating system was used. This is mostly for legacy reasons, and "
"potential debugging information. For more information see "
"[system_info](../concepts/system_info.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:148
msgid "system_info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:148
msgid "The system information object. It replaces the idlver object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:150
msgid "Other Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:152
msgid "gam6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:152
msgid "van der Waals scaling factor (usually 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:153
msgid "h2broad"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:153
msgid "flag determing whether to use H2 broadening or not (usually True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:154
msgid "accrt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:155
msgid ""
"Minimum accuracy for synthethized spectrum at wavelength grid points in "
"`sme.wint` (or SMElib adaptive grid if `sme.wint` is not set). Values "
"below 1e-4 are not meaningful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:158
msgid "accwi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:159
msgid ""
"Minimum accuracy for linear spectrum interpolation vs. wavelength. Values"
" below 1e-4 are not meaningful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:161
msgid "version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:161
msgid "The version of sme used to create this structure and spectrum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:162
msgid "id"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:163
msgid ""
"The date and time when this structure or the last synthetic spectrum was "
"created"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/sme_struct.md:166
msgid ""
"They are called Illiffe vectors in the code, and they were that in IDL. "
"But they are technically not Illiffe vectors anymore, but just lists of "
"individal numpy arrays."
msgstr ""

